### Modern certs + cert-manager plan (tick boxes as you complete)

How to use this checklist
- Tick each box when done to track progress. Replace `[ ]` with `[x]` (or click the checkbox in the editor).
- Aim for the bare minimum to meet goals. Prefer sensible defaults; expose options only where necessary.
- Keep scripts simple, portable Bash; follow the repo's Bash-ninja standards and avoid over-engineering.

---

## Phase 0 — Preconditions and guardrails
- [x] Ensure `openssl` and `bash` are available at runtime. If missing, print a friendly error and exit.
- [x] Add strict mode to all scripts under `src/`: shebang `#!/usr/bin/env bash`, then `set -Eeuo pipefail`, `IFS=$'\n\t'`, and `umask 077` for key material.
- [x] Add traps: `trap 'on_err $LINENO' ERR` and `trap 'on_sig' SIGINT SIGTERM` with minimal handlers printing concise errors (no secrets).
- [x] Implement global option parsing once (quiet/verbose/no-color/non-interactive/help), reusable by subcommands (see `Bash-ninja rules`).
- [x] Implement `.env` loader with precedence: CLI > env > .env > defaults.

Files likely touched
- [x] `src/main.sh` (single entrypoint; subcommands `init`, `issue`, `eject`, `re-init`, `validate`, `version`, `help`)
- [x] `src/common.sh` (shared helpers for parsing, logging, dotenv, path helpers)
- [x] `src/utils.sh` (centralized error handling with filename reporting)

Definition of done for Phase 0
- [x] `bash -n src/*.sh` passes
- [x] `shellcheck src/*.sh` has no errors of severity error

---

## Phase 1 — Modernize certificate generation (avoid `-legacy`)
- [x] Default key type to EC P-256 (`KEY_TYPE=ec`, `EC_CURVE=prime256v1`); allow `KEY_TYPE=rsa` with `RSA_BITS>=3072`.
- [x] Replace legacy keygens with `openssl genpkey` everywhere (root, intermediate, server).
- [x] Store keys in PKCS#8; when encrypting, use PBES2 + AES-256 and PBKDF2 with configurable iterations.
- [x] CSR: use `-sha256`; add SANs via `-addext "subjectAltName = ${SERVER_SANS:-DNS:${SERVER_CN}}"`.
- [x] Signing: `openssl ca -batch -md sha256 -days ${LEAF_DAYS:-398}`; default `LEAF_DAYS=398`.
- [x] PKCS#12 export: use AES and SHA-256 (no legacy provider): `-keypbe AES-256-CBC -certpbe AES-256-CBC -macalg sha256 -iter ${PFX_ITER:-204000} -maciter`.
- [x] PKCS#8 conversion for app-consumed server key: `openssl pkcs8 -topk8 -v2 aes-256-cbc -iter ${PKCS8_ITER:-204000}`.

Files likely touched
- [x] `src/init.sh` (root/intermediate keygen → genpkey; keep sha256; respect KEY_TYPE and defaults)
- [x] `src/request-server-cert.sh` (server keygen → genpkey; SANs; -batch signing; PKCS#8 and PKCS#12 options)

Quick verification (no `-legacy` expected)
- [x] `openssl x509 -noout -text -in <server>.cert.pem | grep -E "Signature Algorithm|Subject Alternative Name"`
- [x] `openssl verify -CAfile ca-chain.cert.pem <server>.cert.pem`
- [x] `openssl pkcs12 -in <server>.pfx -nodes -passin pass:"$PASS" -info >/dev/null`
- [x] `openssl pkcs8 -in <server>.pkcs8.key.pem -passin pass:"$PASS" -nocrypt -out /dev/null`

