## Phase 6 — cert-manager export subcommand (Issuer)
Goal: export artifacts/manifests so Kubernetes cert-manager can use the intermediate CA as a CA Issuer. Do NOT change existing CA layout.

- [ ] Implement `simpleca cert-manager export` subcommand.
- [ ] Options (portable `getopts` with long mappings):
  - [ ] `--ns|--namespace` (required)
  - [ ] `--issuer-name` (default `ca-issuer`)
  - [ ] `--secret-name` (default `ca-key-pair`)
  - [ ] `--out` (default `/opt/export/manifests`)
  - [ ] `--crl` (repeatable)
  - [ ] `--ocsp` (repeatable)
  - [ ] `--force` (allow overwrite)
- [ ] Export unencrypted PKCS#8 intermediate private key into export dir ONLY (never modify `/opt/ca`).
- [ ] Build full chain: `intermediate.cert.pem + root/ca.cert.pem` → `issuer.fullchain.crt.pem`.
- [ ] Render `secret.yaml` with base64 (no wraps): `type: kubernetes.io/tls`, keys: `tls.crt` (full chain), `tls.key` (unencrypted intermediate key).
- [ ] Render `issuer.yaml` that references the Secret; include optional `crlDistributionPoints` and `ocspServers` arrays when provided.
- [ ] Print clear warning that an unencrypted key is written; treat export dir as sensitive.
- [ ] Validation: verify chain, and that intermediate pubkey parses; optional YAML syntax check if `yq` present.

Files likely touched
- [ ] `src/cert-manager.sh` (parse + run)
- [ ] `src/common.sh` (paths: `rootCaCert`, `intermediateKey`, `intermediateCert`, `certificateChain`)

Quick verification
- [ ] `openssl verify -CAfile <root>/ca.cert.pem <intermediate>.cert.pem`
- [ ] `base64 -w0` used for both key and chain in manifests
- [ ] `kubectl apply -f <out>/<ns>/<issuer-name>/secret.yaml` (manual env) succeeds

