Appendix — Minimal commands to copy into scripts (reference only)
- Keygen (EC default):
  - `openssl genpkey -algorithm EC -pkeyopt ec_paramgen_curve:${EC_CURVE:-prime256v1} -pkeyopt ec_param_enc:named_curve -aes-256-cbc -pass pass:"$PASS" -out <path>.key.pem`
- Keygen (RSA option):
  - `openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA -pkeyopt rsa_keygen_bits:${RSA_BITS:-3072} -aes-256-cbc -pass pass:"$PASS" -out <path>.key.pem`
- PKCS#8 (for app/server):
  - `openssl pkcs8 -topk8 -v2 aes-256-cbc -iter ${PKCS8_ITER:-204000} -passin pass:"$PASS" -passout pass:"$PASS" -in <server>.key.pem -out <server>.pkcs8.key.pem`
- PKCS#12 export:
  - `openssl pkcs12 -export -inkey <server>.key.pem -passin pass:"$PASS" -in <server>.cert.pem -certfile <chain>.pem -out <server>.pfx -keypbe AES-256-CBC -certpbe AES-256-CBC -macalg sha256 -iter ${PFX_ITER:-204000} -maciter`
- CA sign (non-interactive):
  - `openssl ca -config <intermediate.cnf> -extensions server_cert -days ${LEAF_DAYS:-398} -notext -md sha256 -batch -passin pass:"$INT_PASS" -in <server>.csr.pem -out <server>.cert.pem`

Notes
- Keep it simple. Prefer sensible defaults; expose only necessary flags.
- Prioritize modern algorithms/formats to eliminate `-legacy`.
- All exports of unencrypted keys must go to explicitly chosen export dirs, never the CA working dir.
